## task-flow bindings
Read by `task-flow:task`, `task-flow:decompose` and `task-flow:ci-gate`.
- **Tracker:** <tracker>. Read a ticket with its comments: `<how>`; comment:
  `<how>`; set Done: `<how>`; log spent time: `<how>`. Token: the **name** of
  the variable (`<VAR_NAME>`), never its value.
- **VCS / CI:** integration branch `<develop>`; open an MR: `<command>`;
  pipeline status: `<command>`; GitLab runner executor: `<docker | shell (tag)>`.
- **Build / verify:** deploy to dev: `<command>`; browser-verify URL: `<url | none>`.
- **Deploy / merge policy:** merge method `<squash | merge>`; approval
  `<self | mr-approval-required>`; MR state: `<glab mr view <id> --output json>`;
  deploy trigger and status: `<how>`.
- **One-way wrappers:** `<make deploy>`, … (handed to `predict on --also`) — or none.
- **Artifact directory:** `docs/specs/` — or `<dir>`.
- **Gate owner:** `@<owner>` — the one identity an MR under check must not be.
- **Builder / reviewer:** each ticket names its builder (`builder: codex | claude`);
  the reviewer is the other harness (`xreview.sh`, task phases 6 and 6b).

